// The difficulty curve: how strong the run's enemy is, by the battle's number, in the player's class's own reference
// army (run::Run::reference — the enemy is the army that reference beats half the time): Forges for the Foundry
// (golems — fractions are a Forge with that share of its health), swarm points for the swarm (ants, a soldier in
// every seven). The same for every run, whatever the player's army: a stronger army wins more often.
// docs/BALANCE.md, «Кривая сложности».
(
    // battles 1..15 (the 5th, 10th and 15th are bosses): about two thirds of what an army of the class that takes
    // its finds brings by then (a start is worth about 3 Forges / 115 points)
    foundry: [2.26, 2.43, 2.54, 2.71, 2.89, 3.35, 3.47, 3.69, 3.81, 3.99, 4.50, 4.62, 4.85, 4.97, 5.09],
    swarm: [80.0, 92.0, 106.0, 120.0, 135.0, 174.0, 192.0, 211.0, 231.0, 252.0, 304.0, 328.0, 353.0, 378.0, 405.0],
    // on top of the battle's own: a dangerous road, an elite, a boss
    danger: 1.15,
    elite: 1.2,
    boss: 1.25,
)
